[al:新概念英语（四）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:The Great Escape]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:01.08]Lesson 47 | 第47课
[00:02.83]The great escape | 大逃亡
[00:10.41]What is one of the features of modern camping where nationality is concerned? | 在国籍方面，现代野营的一个特征是什么？
[00:18.10]Economy is one powerful motive for camping, | 省钱是野营的一个强大动机，
[00:22.33]since after the initial outlay upon equipment, or through hiring it, the total expense can be far less than the cost of hotels. | 因为在最初购置（或租用）装备的花销之后，总开销可以远远低于住旅馆的费用。
[00:34.23]But, contrary to a popular assumption, it is far from being the only one, or even the greatest. | 但与普遍的看法相反，这远非唯一的动机，甚至算不上最大的动机。
[00:44.23]The man who manoeuvres carelessly into his 20 pounds' worth of space at one of Europe's myriad permanent sites may find himself bumping a Bentley. | 在欧洲数不清的常设营地里，谁若漫不经心地把车停进自己那20英镑价位的地盘，没准儿会发现自己蹭上了一辆宾利。
[00:55.54]More likely, Ford Escort will be hub to hub with Renault or Mercedes, but rarely with bicycles made for two. | 更有可能的是，福特“护卫舰”与雷诺或梅赛德斯轮辋挨着轮辋地停放，但很少与双人自行车为邻。
[01:06.19]That the equipment of modern camping becomes yearly more sophisticated is an entertaining paradox for the cynic, | 现代野营的装备一年比一年精巧，这在愤世嫉俗者看来是个有趣的悖论，
[01:15.25]a brighter promise for the hopeful traveller who has sworn to get away from it all. | 而在发誓要摆脱尘世的乐天派旅行者看来，则是一个更光明的前景。
[01:21.14]It also provides--and some student sociologist might care to base his thesis upon the phenomenon--an escape of another kind. | 它还提供了另一种形式的逃避——某位社会学专业的学生或许可以拿这一现象作为论文题目。
[01:33.12]The modern traveller is often a man who dislikes the Splendide and the Bellavista, | 现代旅行者往往不喜欢“豪华饭店”和“美景旅馆”，
[01:39.19]not because he cannot afford, or shuns their material comforts, but because he is afraid of them. | 不是因为他住不起或嫌弃它们的物质享受，而是因为他害怕它们。
[01:47.22]Affluent he may be, but he is by no means sure what to tip the doorman or the chambermaid. | 他也许很富有，却完全不知道该给门房或客房女服务员多少小费。
[01:55.49]Master in his own house he has little idea of when to say boo to a manager hotel. | 在自己家里他说一不二，可到了旅馆经理面前，他就不知道何时该提出异议了。
[02:04.49]From all such fears camping releases him. | 野营把他从所有这些恐惧中解脱出来。
[02:08.23]Granted, a snobbery of camping itself, based upon equipment and techniques, already exists; | 诚然，一种基于装备和技术的野营自身的势利风气已经存在；
[02:16.19]but it is of a kind that, if he meets it, he can readily understand and deal with. | 但这种势利是他一旦遇上就能轻易理解并应付的。
[02:22.93]There is no superior 'they' in the shape of managements and hotel hierarchies to darken his holiday days. | 不存在以经理层和旅馆等级制度面目出现的居高临下的“他们”来败坏他的假日时光。
[02:32.21]To such motives, yet another must be added. | 在这些动机之外，还得再加上一个。
[02:36.45]The contemporary phenomenon of car worship is to be explained not least by the sense of independence and freedom that ownership entails. | 当今崇拜汽车的现象，很大程度上可以由拥车所带来的独立感和自由感来解释。
[02:47.35]To this pleasure camping gives an exquisite refinement. | 野营把这种乐趣提炼得更为精致。
[02:52.24]From one's own front door to home or foreign hills or sands and back again, everything is to hand. | 从自家门口出发，到国内或异国的山峦或海滩再返回，一切都在自己的掌控之中。
[03:01.50]Not only are the means of arriving at the holiday paradise entirely within one's own command and keeping, | 不仅抵达度假天堂的方式完全由自己掌控和保管，
[03:09.13]but the means of escape from holiday hell (if the beach proves too crowded, the local weather too inclement) | 而且从度假地狱逃身的手段（如果海滩过于拥挤，当地天气过于恶劣）
[03:17.68]are there, outside--or, as likely, part of--the tent. | 也近在咫尺，就在帐篷外面——或者很可能就是帐篷的一部分。
[03:25.20]Idealists have objected to the practice of camping, as to the package tour, | 理想主义者反对野营这种做法，就像反对包价旅游一样，
[03:31.06]that the traveller abroad thereby denies himself the opportunity of getting to know the people of the country visited. | 认为出国旅行者因此失去了了解所访国家人民的机会。
[03:38.46]Insularity and self-containment, it is argued, go hand in hand. | 有人争辩说，狭隘与自我封闭是形影不离的。
[03:44.87]The opinion does not survive experience of a popular Continental camping place. | 但这种观点经受不住欧洲大陆一处热门野营地的亲身体验。
[03:50.49]Holiday hotels tend to cater for one nationality of visitors especially, sometimes exclusively. | 度假旅馆往往特别接待某一国籍的游客，有时甚至是唯一的国籍。
[03:59.77]Camping sites, by contrast, are highly cosmopolitan. | 相比之下，野营地则是高度世界性的。
[04:04.55]Granted, a preponderance of Germans is a characteristic that seems common to most Mediterranean sites; | 诚然，德国人占多数似乎是大多数地中海营地共同的特点；
[04:12.51]but as yet there is no overwhelmingly specialized patronage. | 但迄今为止还没有哪个营地被某一国游客压倒性地垄断。
[04:18.28]Notices forbidding the open-air drying of clothes, | 禁止露天晾晒衣物、
[04:21.77]or the use of water points for car washing, | 禁止用水点洗车、
[04:25.30]or those inviting 'our camping friends' to a dance or a boat trip are printed not only in French or Italian or Spanish, but also in English, German and Dutch. | 或邀请“我们的野营朋友”参加舞会或乘船游览的告示，不仅用法语、意大利语或西班牙语印出，还用英语、德语和荷兰语。
[04:37.99]At meal times the odour of sauerkraut vies with that of garlic. | 用餐时分，德国泡菜的气味与大蒜的气味一争高下。
[04:43.13]The Frenchman's breakfast coffee competes with the Englishman's bacon and eggs. | 法国人早餐的咖啡与英国人的熏肉煎蛋互较短长。
[04:49.73]Whether the remarkable growth of organized camping means the eventual death of the more independent kind is hard to say. | 有组织的野营的显著增长是否意味着更独立的那一类最终消亡，这很难说。
[04:58.15]Municipalities naturally want to secure the campers' site fees and other custom. | 市政当局自然想稳稳赚得野营者的营位费及其他光顾。
[05:04.09]Police are wary of itinerants who cannot be traced to a recognized camp boundary or to four walls. | 警方则对那些无法归入某个正规营地范围或四面墙壁之内的流动客心存戒备。
[05:12.15]But most probably it will all depend upon campers themselves: how many heath fires they cause; how much litter they leave; | 但最有可能的是，一切都取决于野营者自己：他们引起多少荒野火灾，留下多少垃圾；
[05:23.04]in short, whether or not they wholly alienate landowners and those who live in the countryside. | 简言之，他们是否彻底疏远了土地所有者和乡村居民。
[05:31.48]Only good scouting is likely to preserve the freedoms so dear to the heart of the eternal Boy Scout. | 只有良好的童子军作风才有可能保住那些令永远的童子军视若珍宝的自由。
